{"conjecture": "Each locally correct modification leaves behind an implicit assumption—some reason it was safe to make—that was never documented because it lived in the heads of the reviewers. When maintainers cycle out, these undocumented epistemic links become invisible tripwires: the code still compiles and tests still pass, but the knowledge of why a change is safe in context is gone. The system grows harder to change not because complexity increases, but because the ratio of surviving tacit constraints to surviving maintainers who hold them deteriorates with every turnover event."}
